WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.002
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.302 --> 00:00:08.653
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.953 --> 00:00:15.449
Unit twenty: AI in Daily Life. Today you will describe things with relative clauses using 'which' and 'that'.

4
00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:18.413
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.367 --> 00:00:22.565
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:25.103
Artificial intelligence.

7
00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:29.544
Artificial intelligence means computers that can think and learn.

8
00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.578
Artificial intelligence helps doctors read X-rays.

9
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:37.637
Your turn. Say: Artificial intelligence.

10
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.337
Artificial intelligence.

11
00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:44.166
Algorithm.

12
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.264
Algorithm means a set of steps a computer follows.

13
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.954
The algorithm chooses the next video.

14
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.144
Your turn. Say: Algorithm.

15
00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.082
Algorithm.

16
00:00:58.817 --> 00:00:59.632
Data.

17
00:01:00.617 --> 00:01:02.628
Data means facts and information.

18
00:01:03.217 --> 00:01:05.147
Apps collect data about us.

19
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.518
Your turn. Say: Data.

20
00:01:11.367 --> 00:01:12.124
Data.

21
00:01:12.883 --> 00:01:14.105
Recommendation.

22
00:01:15.117 --> 00:01:17.174
Recommendation means a suggestion.

23
00:01:17.783 --> 00:01:19.969
The app made a good song recommendation.

24
00:01:20.583 --> 00:01:23.398
Your turn. Say: Recommendation.

25
00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:27.501
Recommendation.

26
00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.483
Voice assistant.

27
00:01:30.483 --> 00:01:34.329
Voice assistant means a program that answers spoken questions.

28
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:37.381
I ask my voice assistant about the weather.

29
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:40.717
Your turn. Say: Voice assistant.

30
00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.079
Voice assistant.

31
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:46.760
Privacy.

32
00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:50.632
Privacy means keeping your information to yourself.

33
00:01:51.217 --> 00:01:52.949
Protect your privacy online.

34
00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.959
Your turn. Say: Privacy.

35
00:01:58.800 --> 00:01:59.801
Privacy.

36
00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:01.539
Benefit.

37
00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:04.491
Benefit means a good result.

38
00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.663
Fast translation is a benefit of AI.

39
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:10.542
Your turn. Say: Benefit.

40
00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:14.320
Benefit.

41
00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:15.933
Risk.

42
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.704
Risk means the chance of something bad happening.

43
00:02:20.317 --> 00:02:22.606
Sharing too much data is a risk.

44
00:02:23.217 --> 00:02:25.741
Your turn. Say: Risk.

45
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:29.485
Risk.

46
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:33.846
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:34.683 --> 00:02:38.331
Visal, how do you use AI in your daily life?

48
00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:43.889
I use a translation app which helps me with English.

49
00:02:44.983 --> 00:02:46.518
Do you know how it works?

50
00:02:47.617 --> 00:02:54.309
It uses an algorithm. An algorithm is a set of steps that solves a problem.

51
00:02:55.417 --> 00:02:56.673
Are there any risks?

52
00:02:57.783 --> 00:03:02.398
Yes. Apps that collect too much data can hurt our privacy.

53
00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:04.999
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.161
Grammar focus: Relative clauses (which and that).

55
00:03:09.461 --> 00:03:10.602
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.317 --> 00:03:14.257
An algorithm is a set of steps that solves a problem.

57
00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.370
I use an app which translates words.

58
00:03:18.283 --> 00:03:20.515
Apps that collect data can be risky.

59
00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.537
Use 'which' or 'that' for things. Use 'who' for people.

60
00:03:25.283 --> 00:03:30.896
Be careful! Don't say: An algorithm is a set of steps who solves a problem.

61
00:03:32.833 --> 00:03:36.540
Say: An algorithm is a set of steps that solves a problem.

62
00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.245
Use 'which' or 'that' for things, and 'who' for people.

63
00:03:40.033 --> 00:03:42.581
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.751
Smart Machines.

65
00:03:45.051 --> 00:03:48.119
Artificial intelligence is part of daily life.

66
00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:52.038
An algorithm is a set of steps that uses data.

67
00:03:53.033 --> 00:03:56.031
It makes a recommendation which matches your interests.

68
00:03:57.033 --> 00:04:00.194
A voice assistant answers the questions that we ask.

69
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.929
AI brings benefits, but also risks for privacy.

70
00:04:06.033 --> 00:04:09.733
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:13.465
An app blank translates words is useful.

72
00:04:13.765 --> 00:04:16.420
A, that. B, who. C, where.

73
00:04:19.967 --> 00:04:21.583
The answer is A: that.

74
00:04:22.717 --> 00:04:25.645
A set of steps a computer follows is an blank.

75
00:04:25.945 --> 00:04:30.434
A, algorithm. B, assistant. C, privacy.

76
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.883
The answer is A: algorithm.

77
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.618
The chance of something bad happening is a blank.

78
00:04:39.918 --> 00:04:43.839
A, risk. B, benefit. C, recommendation.

79
00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:49.283
The answer is A: risk.

80
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.408
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.958
How do you use AI in your daily life?

82
00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.308
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:05:07.608 --> 00:05:16.484
I use a map app that shows me the fastest way to school. I also use a translation app which helps me with new words.

84
00:05:16.784 --> 00:05:18.679
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:19.583 --> 00:05:24.407
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and relative clauses (which and that).

86
00:05:24.707 --> 00:05:30.320
Today's value is critical awareness. Use technology wisely, and always think for yourself.

87
00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:33.318
See you in Unit twenty-one. Goodbye!

88
00:05:33.618 --> 00:05:36.503
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

